Id: no-secret-in-log
Pattern: BreaksTheRule
Subject: *.cs
Except: none
Issue: 80

A metadata source key reaches this plugin through the server's configuration,
and a log line is the shortest route from there to a file an operator pastes
into an issue. The rule is drawn wider than the key itself: anything read out of
configuration is refused in a log statement, because what configuration holds
grows and the log line written today is read again after it does.

The bound is the line. A value put into a variable on one line and logged on the
next is not seen by this rule, and #80 is where the property is held properly
rather than by a pattern.
